{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794429373,"nonce":"xYZh7UxE7mH0o4XQehE7vF8CRb8=","title":"Decide which Pod-level fields k8s_overlay may set (hostAliases, dnsConfig, shareProcessNamespace, hostPID, serviceAccountName, pod securityContext)","message":"Found 2026-11-12 by the audit of d2b711b. Reachable before. Pod-level fields reach Scarab's containers without naming them: hostAliases or dnsConfig can point the server or Depot host at 127.0.0.1, where the step can listen and receive the results and workspace tokens the sidecars send; shareProcessNamespace/hostPID expose sidecar env; serviceAccountName + automount gives API access; hostPath. ADR-0055 calls k8s_overlay the governed escape hatch, so this is a decision on what the grant covers, not only a bug: an allowlist of Pod fields a layer may set, or a list it may not, per layer (operator baseline/profiles vs author overlay).","files":null}]}